Requirement from Max during Hermes c2c dogfooding: readable styling for incoming messages and outgoing send tool calls must cover Hermes TUI and native CLI, not only Telegram. Share semantic envelope/status formatting across surfaces while keeping Telegram/native-entity and TUI/CLI renderers separate. Show sender/recipient, visually distinct literal body, compact metadata, and accurate queued/offline/error/unknown status; never imply queue acceptance proves delivery. Preserve untrusted peer-data boundary, literal markup and multiline/Unicode bodies. Provide usable plain-text output when rich/ANSI unsupported. Telegram custom plugin has working visually approved incoming blockquotes and outgoing receipt cards, but TUI/CLI coverage is not implemented by that artifact. Acceptance: inspect both live TUI and CLI rendering, public regression tests for MCP/native send results and inbound data, long/unicode/hostile markup, non-TTY/plain fallback. Coordinate with existing Hermes integration work and avoid duplicate overlapping task ownership.

Implementation handoff from Hermes coordinator: proven Telegram inbound/outbound formatting lives in /home/xertrov/src/c2c-telegram-plugin at commit 4c6e35b1cf50e771b2d3212516553d596176c21f (bridge.py native entity header/body blockquote and UTF-16 chunking; outbound.py actual Hermes MCP result wrapper decoding, canonical queued body and accurate queue status; test_direct.py/test_outbound.py/test_outbound_boundary.py). This is reusable reference, NOT completed TUI/CLI coverage. Do not copy xsm hardcoded chat ID/profile/grants into bundled plugin. Port shared semantic formatter into data/hermes-plugin, add surface-specific terminal renderers and plain fallback, extend codegen-hermes-plugin file manifest if adding files, regenerate ocaml/cli/c2c_hermes_plugin_embedded.ml and run install/codegen drift tests. Installed ~/.hermes/plugins/c2c is a copied directory, not a symlink; the independent c2c-telegram-inbound is the symlink. Release lane currently active: coordinate ownership and avoid broadening its frozen release; implement B378 serially after release snapshot unless agreed otherwise.

2026-10-23 completion audit: implementation and focused tests are merged, but the original acceptance explicitly requires inspection of live TUI and CLI rendering. The implementation handoff records only offline host-consumer tests and says interactive paint remains unverified. Reopened solely to finish that live validation in owned isolated Hermes sessions; no earlier valid evidence is discarded.

